# ivreg1 with NO user-set limits: the effort defaults now scale with
# the number of parameters (same fix as ivreg opt=3).  In its own file
# because mxit=/nbox= are session settings -- a value set by an earlier
# command in the same file would be inherited, which is exactly the
# respected-user-setting behaviour the main ivreg1.cf pins.
# ivreg1.cf -- t_ireg.c coverage: ivreg1 (interval-data regression via a
# box search, certified minimum). Same data as ivreg2.cf (tdaR's own
# roxygen example values, perturbed slightly to avoid the exact-fit
# degenerate case). Checked structurally: the box search either
# certifies a solution or reports its own status honestly -- tdaR's own
# docs note TDA's default 100/100 iteration/box limits rarely complete
# a real search, so this is not expected to match ivreg2's answer
# exactly, only to run and terminate cleanly.

nvar(
    dfile = ivdat.dat,
    XL [4.1] = c1,
    XH [4.1] = c2,
    YL [4.1] = c3,
    YH [4.1] = c4,
);

ivreg1(tolf=1e-4) = YL,YH,XL,XH;
